{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1436092,
  "courseSlug": "react-native-the-practical-guide",
  "courseTitle": "React Native - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31894934",
      "title": "Understanding Push Notifications",
      "lectureOrder": 252,
      "videoOrder": 243,
      "sourceHash": "fc23d070557ad22aa317deab0ad4459ee3331764c0cc6e7ac44b3861cac3b446",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.11,
          "end": 5.67,
          "en": "So we did explore local Notifications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.67,
          "end": 8.69,
          "en": "which means basically that we're talking to ourselves.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.69,
          "end": 12.04,
          "en": "We're triggering the notification from inside the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.04,
          "end": 15.25,
          "en": "with some code and we're handling the Notification",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.25,
          "end": 16.39,
          "en": "inside the app as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.39,
          "end": 18.84,
          "en": "And it's the same app on the same device",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.84,
          "end": 21.93,
          "en": "that's sending Notifications to itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.93,
          "end": 24.08,
          "en": "But as mentioned before this can be useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.08,
          "end": 26.22,
          "en": "if you're building something like a reminder app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.22,
          "end": 27.453,
          "en": "or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.69,
          "end": 31.02,
          "en": "But of course you also often wanna talk",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.02,
          "end": 34.66,
          "en": "to other instances of the app installed on other devices",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.66,
          "end": 36,
          "en": "by other users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36,
          "end": 39.62,
          "en": "And that's where Push Notifications come into play.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.62,
          "end": 42.34,
          "en": "Because Push Notifications in the end allow you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.295,
          "end": 45.32,
          "en": "to push important, guess what?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.32,
          "end": 48.53,
          "en": "Notifications, so important messages in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.53,
          "end": 52.71,
          "en": "to other devices to notify users of something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.71,
          "end": 55.89,
          "en": "and this something could be a chat message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.89,
          "end": 57.89,
          "en": "but it could also be a marketing message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.89,
          "end": 62.19,
          "en": "sent by the owner of the app to all users of the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.19,
          "end": 63.56,
          "en": "That would be another example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.56,
          "end": 66.25,
          "en": "for a Push Notification as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.25,
          "end": 68.16,
          "en": "But it's very important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.16,
          "end": 71.25,
          "en": "how exactly Push Notifications work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.25,
          "end": 74.38,
          "en": "and what sets them apart from local Notifications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.38,
          "end": 77,
          "en": "though the latter might already be clear.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77,
          "end": 78.9,
          "en": "But how do they work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78.9,
          "end": 82.49,
          "en": "Well, we have our app installed on some device",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.49,
          "end": 86.55,
          "en": "and this app might be talking to a backend owned by us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.55,
          "end": 89.83,
          "en": "to some backend API, but this is not mandatory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.83,
          "end": 92.50999999999999,
          "en": "This is possible, but not required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.50999999999999,
          "end": 95.47999999999999,
          "en": "But of course in many apps you will have some backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.47999999999999,
          "end": 99.87,
          "en": "where some data is stored or some logic is executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.87,
          "end": 102.17,
          "en": "Either way, if you have a backend or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.17,
          "end": 104.7,
          "en": "your app will be doing things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.7,
          "end": 106.94,
          "en": "For example, there might be certain events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 106.94,
          "end": 108.59,
          "en": "that occur in your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 108.59,
          "end": 111.973,
          "en": "Maybe a chat message was sent, if it's a chat app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.03999999999999,
          "end": 115.93,
          "en": "Events might also occur on your backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.93,
          "end": 117.41,
          "en": "though if you have one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 117.41,
          "end": 120.2,
          "en": "Again, it's not required but if you have a backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.2,
          "end": 123.04,
          "en": "events could occur there as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.04,
          "end": 125.77,
          "en": "Either that chat message that's being stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.77,
          "end": 127.82,
          "en": "in a database, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.82,
          "end": 130.81,
          "en": "That could be an event that occurs on the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 130.81,
          "end": 133.03,
          "en": "or maybe you as the app owner",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.03,
          "end": 135.22,
          "en": "decide to send a marketing message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 135.22,
          "end": 138.04,
          "en": "to all installed instances of your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 138.04,
          "end": 140.7,
          "en": "So to all users of your app, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 140.7,
          "end": 143.52,
          "en": "and that of course also would be kind of an event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 143.52,
          "end": 146.04,
          "en": "occurring on the backend that you as the owner",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 146.04,
          "end": 148.483,
          "en": "decide to send a marketing message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 149.72,
          "end": 153.52,
          "en": "Either way, upon certain events you might want to send",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 153.52,
          "end": 156.95,
          "en": "a notification to other instances of the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 156.95,
          "end": 158.87,
          "en": "installed on other devices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 158.87,
          "end": 160.77,
          "en": "Either because of events that occurred",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 160.77,
          "end": 162.53,
          "en": "on the app on one device,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 162.53,
          "end": 165.19299999999998,
          "en": "or because of events that occurred on the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 166.21,
          "end": 170.8,
          "en": "So the goal with Push Notifications is to send messages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 170.8,
          "end": 173.84,
          "en": "Notifications to other devices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 173.84,
          "end": 177.49,
          "en": "So to your app installed on other devices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 177.49,
          "end": 180.92,
          "en": "And this could be one device that's being targeted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 180.92,
          "end": 183.01,
          "en": "but it could also be multiple devices,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 183.01,
          "end": 185.68,
          "en": "maybe thousands of devices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 185.68,
          "end": 188.5,
          "en": "This really depends on the kind of message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 188.5,
          "end": 191.02,
          "en": "If you're sending a chat message to a friend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 191.02,
          "end": 191.94,
          "en": "and you wanna send",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 191.94,
          "end": 194.57,
          "en": "a push notification to that friend's phone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 194.57,
          "end": 197.7,
          "en": "to make him or her aware of that message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 197.7,
          "end": 199.97,
          "en": "then the Push Notification will be sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 199.97,
          "end": 201.82999999999998,
          "en": "to one device, probably.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 201.82999999999998,
          "end": 205.54,
          "en": "To your friend's device where the app is installed on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 205.54,
          "end": 209.03,
          "en": "Of course, if you're posting into a group chat",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 209.03,
          "end": 212.22,
          "en": "a Push Notification might be sent to multiple devices",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 212.22,
          "end": 213.56,
          "en": "for all your friends",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 213.56,
          "end": 216.42000000000002,
          "en": "that are in one and the same chat group.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 216.42000000000002,
          "end": 218.749,
          "en": "So it depends on the kind of message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 218.749,
          "end": 221.2,
          "en": "how many devices it is delivered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 221.2,
          "end": 224.36,
          "en": "but the idea behind Push Notifications always is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 224.36,
          "end": 226.89,
          "en": "that it's being delivered to a different device",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 226.89,
          "end": 229.07,
          "en": "than the device on which it originated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 229.07,
          "end": 231.32999999999998,
          "en": "So on which the event occurred.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 231.32999999999998,
          "end": 233.41,
          "en": "So we wanna send such a notification",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 233.41,
          "end": 236.04,
          "en": "either from one app instance on one device,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 236.04,
          "end": 238.37,
          "en": "to another app instance on another device",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 238.37,
          "end": 242.05,
          "en": "or from our backend to some devices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 242.05,
          "end": 245.66,
          "en": "But this is not possible like this, our apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 245.66,
          "end": 249.53,
          "en": "and also our backends can't directly send Notifications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 249.53,
          "end": 251.42,
          "en": "like this to other devices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 251.42,
          "end": 252.713,
          "en": "This does not work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 253.62,
          "end": 256.21,
          "en": "This does not work for security reasons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 256.21,
          "end": 258.503,
          "en": "and also to prevent spam and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 259.483,
          "end": 262.57,
          "en": "And therefore both Google and Apple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 262.57,
          "end": 266.44,
          "en": "in the end both force you to use some backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 266.44,
          "end": 269.9,
          "en": "provided by them to send Push Notifications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 269.9,
          "end": 272.06,
          "en": "to other devices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 272.06,
          "end": 276.36,
          "en": "So you need to go over some Push Notification Servers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 276.36,
          "end": 278.92,
          "en": "to send those Notifications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 278.92,
          "end": 282.87,
          "en": "Now, Apple and Google force you to take this extra route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 282.87,
          "end": 285.84000000000003,
          "en": "but actually such Push Notification Servers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 285.84000000000003,
          "end": 290.71,
          "en": "are also provided by other providers, for example, Expo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 290.71,
          "end": 291.90999999999997,
          "en": "Under the hood though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 291.90999999999997,
          "end": 295.81,
          "en": "Expo is talking to Apple's and Google's servers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 295.81,
          "end": 300.06,
          "en": "but using servers like Expo's Push Notification Server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 300.06,
          "end": 302.4,
          "en": "allows you to talk to one server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 302.4,
          "end": 305.32,
          "en": "to send push notifications to multiple devices",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 305.32,
          "end": 307.46,
          "en": "running multiple operating systems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 307.46,
          "end": 310.163,
          "en": "So to Android and iOS at the same time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 311.09,
          "end": 314.11,
          "en": "So therefore you must send a message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 314.11,
          "end": 316.2,
          "en": "an HTTP request in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 316.2,
          "end": 318.89,
          "en": "to such a Push Notification Server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 318.89,
          "end": 322.34,
          "en": "to have that server deliver a Push Notification",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 322.34,
          "end": 325.61,
          "en": "to the devices where your app is installed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 325.61,
          "end": 327.67,
          "en": "And you can send such a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 327.67,
          "end": 329.92,
          "en": "to the Push Notification Server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 329.92,
          "end": 332.33,
          "en": "either from inside your backend code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 332.33,
          "end": 336.37,
          "en": "If you had an event that occurred in your backend code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 336.37,
          "end": 338.71,
          "en": "or directly from inside your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 338.71,
          "end": 341.55,
          "en": "and I will show you the latter in this course section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 341.55,
          "end": 343.83299999999997,
          "en": "but both approaches are possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 344.71,
          "end": 347.47,
          "en": "And then it's the Push Notification Server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 347.47,
          "end": 351.67,
          "en": "and under the hood, therefore Google's and Apple's servers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 351.67,
          "end": 355.14,
          "en": "that will actually reach out to the actual devices",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 355.14,
          "end": 359.72,
          "en": "and deliver the Push Notifications to those devices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 359.72,
          "end": 363.42,
          "en": "And then on those devices, the notification will arrive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 363.42,
          "end": 366.48,
          "en": "just as the local notification arrived.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 366.48,
          "end": 368.88,
          "en": "So there you can handle it in the same way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 368.88,
          "end": 372.87,
          "en": "as mentioned before, but it's delivered to those devices",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 372.87,
          "end": 376.13,
          "en": "from Google's and Apple's Push Notifications Servers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 376.13,
          "end": 378.34,
          "en": "which in turn can be targeted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 378.34,
          "end": 381.41,
          "en": "with help of Expo's Push Notification Server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 381.41,
          "end": 383.443,
          "en": "simply to simplify things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 384.32,
          "end": 385.59,
          "en": "So that's the big picture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 385.59,
          "end": 389.79,
          "en": "And if it's still not 100% clear yet, that's no problem",
          "zh": ""
